{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `k1`, `k2`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observations are top-level data variables and are each observed exactly once with plain built-in `binomial` sampling statements. The context inputs `n1` and `n2` are used only as binomial trial counts and generated-quantity bounds.
","model_safe_stan":"// Inferring a Common Rate, With Posterior Predictive
data {
  int<lower=1> n1;
  int<lower=1> n2;
  int<lower=0> k1;
  int<lower=0> k2;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0, upper=1> theta;
}
model {
  // Prior on Single Rate Theta
  theta ~ beta(1, 1);

  // Observed Counts
  k1 ~ binomial(n1, theta);
  k2 ~ binomial(n2, theta);
}
generated quantities {
  int<lower=0, upper=n1> postpredk1;
  int<lower=0, upper=n2> postpredk2;

  // Posterior Predictive
  postpredk1 = binomial_rng(n1, theta);
  postpredk2 = binomial_rng(n2, theta);
}

","data_safe_json":"{
  "k1": 2,
  "k2": 2,
  "n1": 4,
  "n2": 2
}
","protected_variables":["k1","k2"]}
